# Fixed 2026-10-01, defect 138, lane emit: the shape beside the first, a mark
# the AUTHOR adds where the library writes none.
# Symptom: `hero_str_try_from_cstr(p: cstr lent, ...)` against the library's
# `p: cstr` stopped `check` with `internal error`, at the library's line 123,
# exit 2.
# Cause: the one `contract_differs` put at the later declaration of a pair,
# the library's. The repair holds every declaration to the library's and
# puts the caret here.

extern "heroes_runtime.h"  #~ ffi_runtime_header
    function hero_str_try_from_cstr(p: cstr lent, @status: i64) -> str  #~ contract_differs

function main()
    print("hello")

# Corrected 2026-10-29, defect 2256 (panel 232's R6): no program names
# `heroes_runtime.h` since, and the library binds `hero_str_try_from_cstr` from
# `hero_os.h`, so the group above is refused at its string as well; the
# contract this case holds to the library's stands as it did.
